    {
      "ordinal": 7,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "2.1",
      "title": "Historical sources and datation",
      "body": "● The sources provide the following available materials during the middle ages:\n○ Linen ○ Wool ○ Silk ○ Coton.\n● Those materials are approved for 14th-century, Transitional armors and 15th-century armors.\n● Depending on the area and time-period, other textiles fibers may be available. Any other material based on historical sources can be accepted.\n● Textiles were used in many applications, such as:\n○ Tabard ○ Covering a coat of plates, corazzina or brigantine ○ Gambesons ○ Chausses ○ Helmet decoration (burlet, torse, orle, crest etc.).",
      "page_from": 4,
      "page_to": 4,
      "stable_key": "textile-and-leather:2.1",
      "parent_key": "textile-and-leather:2",
      "review_status": "extracted",
